62
00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:48.920
First, what do you believe? It's important to find out what the other person

63
00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:49.660
believes.

64
00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:56.860
Proverbs 18:13 says it is foolish and shameful to answer before you hear.

65
00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:03.400
to have an honest conversation with somebody we first have to understand what that

66
00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:08.580
person really believes and that person is only going to share what they believe when

67
00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:14.240
we ask good questions and really listen second why do you believe it what

68
00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:20.220
reasons does the person have for his or her beliefs Proverbs 20 verse 5 says that

69
00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:25.600
the purpose in a man's heart is like deep water but it takes a person of

70
00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.820
understanding who can draw it out.

71
00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:33.920
In other words, people have deep reasons for why they believe as they do and

72
00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.700
sometimes people know those reasons sometimes they don't.

73
00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:42.280
Take my father for example before he became a Christian he was an angry agnostic.

74
00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:47.320
He looked for ways to shoot Christians down and prove that they were wrong.

75
00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:51.820
One thing he didn't fully realize at the time is he would hear people talk about a

76
00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.740
Heavenly Father and he thought why would I want a Heavenly Father.

77
00:05:54.980 --> 00:06:00.160
That idea turned him off. Why? Because his earthly father was abusive

78
00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:05.380
and absent. His relationship with his father was a deep reason

79
00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:08.780
that gave him some anger against God.

80
00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:14.960
People have deep reasons for why they believe as they do, and it takes wisdom and

81
00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:20.320
listening and patience to help draw out what those real reasons often are.

82
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:26.740
The third question is where do we agree where can we find common ground

83
00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:32.460
finding common ground is a powerful way to have meaningful spiritual conversations

84
00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:38.360
with other people when we find common ground often someone's guard will go down and

85
00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:42.680
they'll listen in a way they wouldn't have listened before when i was meeting with

86
00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:47.120
these skeptics they were surprised to find out even though we clearly differ on a

87
00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:52.980
number of significant issues how much we actually have in common and the

88
00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:58.380
fourth question is where do we disagree I've had at least two

89
00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:03.660
significant spiritual conversations with skeptics about the origin of the universe

90
00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:08.160
and each of these conversations we talked about the science and the philosophy that

91
00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.760
points towards the universe having a beginning as we got back to really the

92
00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:17.700
basis of the argument, I said to him, I said, either you have to believe that the

93
00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:22.560
universe can come into existence from nothing or you believe there's a cause outside

94
00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:26.640
of space, outside of time that speaks the universe into existence.

95
00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.940
Which do you find more reasonable?

96
00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:34.540
And both of them looked me right in the eyes and said, a universe from nothing is

97
00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:39.020
most reasonable. Now, in some ways, I'm not exactly sure where to take the argument

98
00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:44.640
from that. So I just said back to him i said okay here's where you and i differ i

99
00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:48.800
think it's more reasonable there's a god who speaks the universe into existence you

100
00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:54.360
think it's more reasonable that something can come from nothing all i was trying to

101
00:07:54.360 --> 00:08:00.280
do was clarify the cost of being an atheist now interestingly in

102
00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:05.940
a matter of time one of them actually became a believer in my

103
00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:11.380
experience most people are willing to have genuine spiritual conversations

104
00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:16.580
if we treat people the way they want to be treated they'll often return the favor to

105
00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:22.420
us if we really listen to people and value their opinions most people will listen

106
00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:27.920
back and value what we have to say as well you have learned some powerful

107
00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:33.860
lessons in this study and you are ready for spiritual conversations now I don't

108
00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.680
think you have to have all the answers.

109
00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.560
I don't have even close to all the answers.

110
00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:42.860
If someone asks you a tough question, just simply say, I don't know, and then go

